<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Mesopotamia and Iran</p><h1 class="st-title">Zengid dynasty of Mosul</h1><p class="st-meta">1127 CE – 1233 CE · capital Mosul</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The senior line of the Zengids, who ruled Mosul after Zengi's capture of Edessa and left the city its great Nuri mosque.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1127 the Seljuk sultan appointed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imad-al-din-zengi">Imad al-Din Zengi</a> atabeg of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosul">Mosul</a>. Zengi added <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a> in 1128 and captured <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-edessa">Edessa</a> in 1144, destroying the County of Edessa and provoking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-crusade">Second Crusade</a>. After his murder in 1146 his lands were divided: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nur-al-din">Nur al-Din</a> took Aleppo and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a>, forming the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/zengid-dynasty">Zengid dynasty</a>, while Mosul passed to his son Sayf al-Din <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazi">Ghazi</a> I.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosul">Mosul</a> <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/zengid-dynasty">Zengids</a> were Turkish rulers of an Arab, Kurdish and Christian population, governing through atabeg households and patronising <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a> learning, architecture and metalwork, for which Mosul was famed. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qutb-al-din-mawdud">Qutb al-Din Mawdud</a> ruled from 1149 to 1170. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-mosque-of-al-nuri-mosul">Great Mosque of al-Nuri</a>, built by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nur-al-din">Nur al-Din</a> in 1172 with its leaning al-Hadba minaret, stood until its destruction in 2017.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/izz-al-din-masud-i">Izz al-Din Mas'ud</a> to accept Ayyubid overlordship in 1186. The last Zengid rulers became figureheads for their minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badr-al-din-lulu">Badr al-Din Lu'lu'</a>, who took power around 1233, founding the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/luluid-dynasty">Lu'lu'id dynasty</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 1127 CE – 1233 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesopotamia and Iran</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:82.13%;width:2.11%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1127 CE – 1233 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mosul</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Imad al-Din Zengi, Qutb al-Din Mawdud, Nur al-Din Arslan Shah I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic, Turkic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/iraq">Iraq</a>, <a href="/countries/syria">Syria</a>, <a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Zengids of Mosul, Zengid atabegate of Mosul</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1180&amp;focus=zengid-dynasty-of-mosul" aria-label="Zengid dynasty of Mosul on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5765 867 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Zengid dynasty of Mosul lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6085 1123L6231 1174M6085 1123L5811 1337M6085 1123L6085 1123M6085 1123L6108 1128"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6231 1174h0M5811 1337h0M6085 1123h0M6108 1128h